        "original_id": "7f2ed5b1-6c80-53d2-88bd-ca0669722c57",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Benny Andersson, Björn Ulvaeus\n- Groups: ABBA\n- Songs: \"Money, Money, Money\", \"That's Me\"\n- Albums: \"Arrival\"\n- Musicals: \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", \"Mamma Mia!\"\n- Places: Japan\n\nFacts:\n- Benny Andersson was born on 16 December 1946.\n- Benny Andersson is a Swedish musician, composer, and member of the Swedish music group ABBA from 1972 to 1982.\n- Benny Andersson co-composed the musicals \"Chess\", \"Kristina från Duvemåla\", and \"Mamma Mia!\".\n- ABBA recorded the song \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- Benny Andersson and Björn Ulvaeus wrote the song \"Money, Money, Money\".\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" was released as a single the year after the \"Arrival\" album release to promote ABBA's album \"Arrival\".\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" was released with \"Money, Money, Money\" as its B-side.\n- In Japan, \"That's Me\" reached number 75 on the official Japanese charts.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
